on in Prague showcases the stories of partisans and soldiers whose fates barely received any attention for decades.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Bulgaria, record low voter turnout triggers a November 1 presidential run-off in a poll colored by divisions over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a04b75f6a46025b2067779d29588ddbf0562c32abf8e1a5410d8458713ec8f83</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by/a-79753496--78ae87f6d8b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Low voter turnout has triggered a run-off for the Bulgarian presidency. The vote was colored by strong divisions over Russia's war in Ukraine, and Sofia's relations with the Kremlin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's new deal on Mediterranean maritime boundaries with Libya is exacerbating issues with Greece and the EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:760b02092c242317efcd12f6cc0fde7a42671f43ae6ced2fd670b8233498849b</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece/a-79745971--8e4f859a6229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece-and-the-eu/a-79745971?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Libya plan to redraw maritime boundaries in the Mediterranean as part of a new economic corridor. This has sparked strong protests from Greece, and has also drawn the European Union into the conflict.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's attacks on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, are intensifying. DW asked people on the ground what life is like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf79dd562c99f7953eb27160e7da946501122a9eae6e78a3c121415f123e3ad</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-/a-79741090--9d6ca1b7b337.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-is-like/a-79741090?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's attacks on the Ukrainian capital are hitting harder and more frequently, making 2026 one of the long war's bloodiest years for Kyiv. DW asked people on the ground what life is like.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine tries to shut Moscow's airports with drone strikes on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d54d247c307daa95b2597e852104c3cac802bb3b4008e3f584570f8081239b9</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469--16f9cb7db516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Repeated Ukrainian drone attacks are increasingly disrupting operations at Moscow's airports. The pounding is part of Ukraine's plan to shut down Russia's airpace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Hope, tension and apprehension as voters prepare to elect new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2c5b21c0bf186c742fac0d0d98127f599bb6c8d27c7f0ab5cfa85f25d912bfa</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102--35e507b36c9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of protests, Serbia faces a pivotal election on Sunday, with a student-led challenge to Aleksandar Vucic's lengthy rule. Allegations of electoral irregularities and fears of a post-election crisis abound.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Tens of thousands rally ahead of elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6eec3f0b7850f282fcbad57829c012f8f516de035759ca1b9d4534d439b68b6</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T03:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-tens-of-thousands-rally-ahead-of-elections/a-79738420--6d4a0cffd723.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-tens-of-thousands-rally-ahead-of-elections/a-79738420?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of student-led protests, Serbia will soon vote in what observers describe as a referendum-like snap election pitting strongman Aleksandar Vucic against the student movement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania's student protests are only getting bigger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c6385d20298c2e5fcc7a332f18dff644a2e76a0afee25079d7a32c723b4659c</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-s-student-protests-are-only-getting-bigger/a-79735213--609bd8634d9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-s-student-protests-are-only-getting-bigger/a-79735213?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As police try to suppress anti-corruption protests by young Albanians, Prime Minister Edi Rama is claiming that "antifa" is behind the unrest. Few are buying that explanation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are the French police the most violent in the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efb8a2937d9afaf9b245ddad36658c04305dcf53cfe97c2c54da34de13bec373</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855--34f0b0f7045e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As protests continue in France, the French police are under scrutiny after new allegations of police brutality. The force has a bigger arsenal than most in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Life near the front line in Sloviansk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d5e5ca522ea03e6013125c9a249afec529a01cdaaaed9edbfe8a370fe6f46b1</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636--5ef08a6d884a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russian continues to attack Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine, thousands of residents refuse to leave or struggle to find a way out. For many, poverty, family ties and beloved pets make evacuation painfully difficult.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Concerns about security in the Black Sea dominate presidential election campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a50015ea99c54b43abb309fbef5bd5d16fc19009c115851b3af0328692e6ce4d</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094--fc0e44625feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgaria's presidential election campaign has been shaped by recent drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea and the government's reduced support for Ukraine, making foreign policy a key factor in the first round.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Putin and Xi at one table, without Ukraine. What Moscow wants from the proposal and why Beijing might agree.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adbba5cccec070cdb6f477007df9c4ab48eb8efea553ea67ee8eab64a727427b</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-/a-79726190--eeff17927fb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-might-agree/a-79726190?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is pushing for a summit with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping to discuss ending the war in Ukraine, without Kyiv or the EU. What does Russia hope to gain, and why might China be willing to take part?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Raids at far-right group's offices at European Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f23606000fa39b1bdf9d596e7d21754e0bb68792fde794e385f1aebbc64a889</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631--002ed5188c2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities searched the Patriots for Europe's European Parliament offices in a long-running funding inquiry. The group says the charges pertain to its predecessor and there is "no legal continuity" between the two.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests German man, calls him a Ukraine 'mercenary'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:230b31f633730bc3ce33e6be3acd9abc70bc091dc93eb2ff213105c01e234018</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871--8b55608360c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian FSB agents have arrested a German national and accused him of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine's military. They claim he deserted over unpaid wages and say he was a sniper who once served in the Bundeswehr.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia frees jailed American Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49c58864853fc7c1dc4aabc330950c3a3076260fdbcf9fb89ad19aec01237723</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452--b6488d619654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During talks between Vladimir Putin and Steve Witkoff, Putin announced that jailed American Stephen Hubbard had been released. The Kremlin also said Russia was "in principle" ready to resume trilateral talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New EU plan for Arctic warily eyes influence of Russia, US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4a96cc27b73b140042fee3fb9f3155d377fe4590619f269f0221fd35c557647</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219--7030ab283919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU unveiled its priorities in the Arctic as it vies with Russia, China and the US for influence. EU foreign affairs chief Kaja Kallas said drone incursions, GPS jamming and cable sabotage undermine Arctic security.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89a72fa638fd2a23c47b7d983ac145b454a4ff3f08bc19a85a6bb126e4544b24</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What Earth's sixth mass extinction event means for humans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e88f2293ecfe8d68ac58a288830bc332bcf5988e24bfe0798390ca14e6d9325</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410--0a12d110aea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human activity is driving plants and animals to extinction at an unprecedented rate. As countries meet in Armenia to discuss ways to reverse nature loss, DW reveals how declining biodiversity is already harming people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>France: Young voters blase about Glucksmann's Socialists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0c74ee2686bd5622851cbe7450eac76fac49e1d60e47145b2131f09dd65c8a0</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159--5c98176d41f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Raphael Glucksmann wants to lead France's Socialists to power without working with the left-populist Jean-Luc Melenchon, who is particularly popular with young voters. How can the center-left candidate win them over?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
